7"}],"id":"fnref:zip-0317"},"; \"zatoshi\" is as defined in the Zcash protocol specification. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"href":"#fn:protocol"}],"id":"fnref:protocol"}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP cuts ZIP 317's ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"href":"#fn:zip-0317"}],"id":"fnref2:zip-0317"}," ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑚"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑟"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑔"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑛"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑙"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑓"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]}]}]}," from 5,000 to 1,000 zatoshis per logical action, so the minimum conventional fee drops from 10,000 to 2,000 zatoshis. It also raises ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑔"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["ℎ"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑡"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑟"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑡"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑜"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑐"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑝"]}]}]}," in ZIP 317's block template algorithm from 4 to 10, so that the fee cut does not narrow the range as sharply. Nothing else in ZIP 317 changes."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["ZIP 317's fee was set in late 2022, when ZEC was about USD 30 and the minimum fee of 10,000 zatoshis cost about USD 0.0030. The fee is fixed in zatoshis, so when the price went up, so did the fee. At about USD 1,300 (the price on 2026-10-21), the minimum fee costs about USD 0.13."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Cutting ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑚"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑟"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑔"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑛"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑙"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑓"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]}]}]}," to 1,000 brings the minimum fee to 2,000 zatoshis, about USD 0.026. Even after a 5x cut, it is still about 8.7 times what it was when ZEC was about USD 30. It only gets cheaper than the 2022 fee if ZEC falls below about USD 150."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Additionally, ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑔"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["ℎ"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑡"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑟"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑡"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑜"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑐"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑝"]}]}]}," is a multiple of the conventional fee, so cutting ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑚"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑟"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑔"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑛"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑙"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑓"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]}]}]}," shrinks the range of inclusion-influencing fees from 10,000 - 40,000 zatoshis to 2,000 - 8,000. Raising ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑒"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝑖"]},{"tag":"mi",